True. But I think with respect to NetHack undead types, it might be
possible to agree on certain source myths. Zombies seem to be an invention
of B-Movies, where it's mostly either an "infection", or some natural
catastrophe-like event that makes the dead come alive no matter how they
died, I think. So resurrection as a Zombie makes sense.
For vampires, it's even clearer. Most vampire fiction involves the bite of
a vampire turning the victim into a vampire.
Liches are a kind of voluntary undead, so Lich-ness shouldn't be contagious
(and it isn't).

> WRT mummies one can *construct* an explanation; to have been victim of
